Among the architects of modern technology, John von Neumann (Father of the Computer), Alan Turing (proposer of the Turing machine), and Claude Shannon (Father of Information Theory/Communication) are undoubtedly god-like figures. But why does Wittgenstein hold such a transcendent status in the history of thought?
